ly / founder-controlled|","p":1}}],"tabs":{"cos":{"title":"The World's Largest News Organisations","about":"The biggest news producers and distributors worldwide, sized by global news reach — from wire agencies that feed everyone to the platforms that now decide what most people see. Together these cover the great majority of global news reach. <span class=\"mono\">(2026)</span>","size":"Marker size = approximate global news reach/scale (tiers). Reach figures come from Reuters Institute, Press Gazette/Similarweb and company data (2025). There is no single summable 'share of world news' (unlike ad dollars), so entries are sized by reach, not market share. This set spans essentially all the world's largest news outlets plus the platforms most people use to find news."},"own":{"title":"Who Controls the World's News","about":"The biggest owners of news — the states, families, funds and platforms that control the outlets and the distribution. Sized by breadth of news control. <span class=\"mono\">(2026)</span>","size":"Marker size = approximate breadth of news control. States and founder-families dominate editorial control; index funds are the largest shareholders of listed news firms; platforms control distribution, not newsrooms."}}}